    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "Churches Estate Agents are delighted to present No. 35 Willow Vale, Ballybrack to the market. This beautifully maintained and thoughtfully extended three-bedroom family home enjoys a superb position on a quiet cul-de-sac directly opposite Ballybrack Shopping Centre.\r\n\r\nLovingly cared and upgraded for by its current owners this attractive property combines generous accommodation with a stylish interior, warm and a wonderful sense of space. \r\nExtended to both the front and rear the home offers excellent family living accommodation together with a number of standout features including a south west facing rear garden, guest WC, large garden shed, off-street parking and an electric car charger.\r\n\r\nApproached via an open driveway with ample off-street parking this property immediately makes a welcoming first impression. On entering the unusually spacious L-shaped hallway features beautiful herringbone wood flooring which continues into the elegant sitting room.\r\nThis comfortable reception room is centered around a risky bold colour tone with an open fire creating a warm and inviting atmosphere. Continuing through the hallway a convenient guest WC is tucked neatly beneath the stairs. To the rear lies the heart of the home with an\r\nimpressive open-plan family space incorporating the kitchen, dining and living areas. This bright and versatile large room is perfectly suited to modern family life and entertaining with an excellent range of fitted kitchen units, gas hob, built-in electric oven, extensive countertop space and generous room for family dining and relaxation.\r\n\r\nUpstairs, the same tasteful décor and balanced tones continue throughout the accommodation. There are three well-proportioned bedrooms comprising two doubles and one single all benefiting from fitted wardrobes and wood flooring. Both double bedrooms positioned to the front and rear of the property enjoy two windows allowing for amounts of natural light. The spacious family bathroom is fitted with a three-piece suite and features a pumped rainfall-effect shower over the bath complemented by an extra-wide window.\r\n\r\nA particularly useful bonus attic space is accessed via steep 'boat stairs' from this level. Currently used for storage this area benefits from wood flooring and a Velux window and offers exciting potential for further use. It could lend itself perfectly to a home office, playroom, guest space or hobby room.\r\n\r\nOutside, the south west facing rear garden provides a wonderful private space for outdoor entertaining, family activities and enjoying the sunshine. A large garden shed provides valuable additional storage and has electric and plumbing.\r\n\r\nWillow Vale is ideally positioned in Ballybrack directly adjoining Kilbogget Park, where residents and locals can enjoy an excellent choice of sporting and recreational facilities including GAA, soccer and rugby. The park's perimeter also provides walking and running routes through its extensive green spaces.\r\n\r\nThe location is exceptionally well connected with regular bus services available along Churchview Road. The DART is accessible from nearby stations (Glenageary & Killiney) while the LUAS is available at Cherrywood. Killiney Beach is also within easy reach offering the opportunity to enjoy the coastline and popular sea swimming spots. Families are well catered for with a choice of schools in the surrounding area. Excellent road connectivity puts the M50 and N11 within 2x mins drive together with easy access to the QBC.\r\n\r\nViewing is highly recommended."
      },
